<h1>Help</h1><div class="box prose">
<h2>Daily routine</h2><ol><li>Open <a href="/admin/orders?status=awaiting_dispatch">Orders awaiting dispatch</a>. Print the packing slip, pack, then set the status to Packed / Dispatched and enter the courier and tracking number.</li>
<li>When the customer receives it, set Delivered. For pay-on-delivery orders, press “Record cash collected”.</li><li>Check Low stock on the dashboard and order from your suppliers (Suppliers &amp; purchases).</li><li>Record today's expenses (Expenses).</li></ol>
<h2>Money words</h2><ul><li><strong>Sales (revenue)</strong>: what customers paid. Not profit.</li><li><strong>Gross profit</strong>: selling price minus what the perfume cost you.</li><li><strong>Margin</strong>: gross profit ÷ selling price. <strong>Markup</strong>: gross profit ÷ cost. They are different numbers.</li><li><strong>Net operating profit (estimate)</strong>: gross profit + delivery fees collected − refunds − payment fees − all expenses you recorded. Only as accurate as the costs and expenses you record.</li><li><strong>Cash</strong>: money that actually moved. Buying stock is cash out but not an expense until it is sold.</li></ul>
<h2>Stock rules</h2><p>Stock is held (reserved) when an order is placed and leaves the shelf when the order is paid (online) or dispatched (pay-on-delivery). Unpaid online orders release their stock after the time set in Settings. Every manual change needs a reason and is recorded.</p>
<h2>Roles</h2><p>Owner: everything. Manager: everything except Settings and Staff. Sales: orders, customers, deliveries. Inventory: products, stock and suppliers.</p></div>
